First Author: Nosoudi
Title: Leveraging machine learning to predict de novo skin malignancy following lung transplantation
Source number: 78

Very short summary: This retrospective US national-registry study analysed 30,917 lung transplant recipients without a documented pretransplant malignancy using pre-, peri-, and post-transplant variables. Multiple supervised machine-learning algorithms were evaluated with a 70:30 internal split and SMOTE; Gradient Boosting performed best for overall de novo malignancy prediction, with a held-out test AUC of 0.746, and also achieved the highest AUC for skin versus non-skin malignancy classification.

