	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: Gradient Boosting was compared with Random Forest, decision-tree variants, logistic-regression variants, LARS, neural networks, and SVM. The dataset was randomly divided into 70% training and 30% testing subsets. Variables were screened using clinical relevance, redundancy, missingness above 30%, association with the outcome, and intervariable correlation, reducing 580 variables to 407. Gradient Boosting parameters including iterations, sampling proportion, and shrinkage were tuned. Interpretation was provided through ranked validation-importance scores for individual predictors.

